activities.description:
The programme will strengthen African AI ecosystems to develop and apply AI responsibly with investments across: 
•	AI policy and governance research – supporting Africa-based institutes to research the risks and governance challenges to inform national AI policies and regulation;
•	AI talent and skills – including interdisciplinary post-graduate AI research hubs at African universities;
•	Machine-learning ready datasets – improving access to datasets for AI models and applications;
•	AI innovation – supporting networks of African innovators to develop high-impact AI solutions to development challenges, exploring the untapped potential of Generative AI to create leapfrogging opportunities for Africa.
•	Scaling AI impact – catalysing financing to take the most promising innovations to scale.

All of the above activities will have a strong focus on responsible AI and on gender and inclusion.
